    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d342-a1">

                <pb facs="0634" n="540" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg540"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Colonial office to foreign office</hi>. (<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                        June</hi> 17.)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Downing Street</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-06-17"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 17,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the letter from this
                    department of the 27th April, relating to the treatment of the United States
                    fishing vessels <hi rendition="#italic">Laura Sayward</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Jenny Seaverns</hi>, I am directed by Secretary Sir
                    Henry’ Holland to transmit to you, to be laid before the Marquis of Salisbury,
                    for such action as he may think proper to take upon it, a copy of a dispatch
                    from the governor-general of Canada, with an affidavit by the master of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Laura Sayward</hi>.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bramston.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
